---
description: Pedagogy-first AI tutor (v2) — hard product and engineering rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Tutor behaviour (ask-before-tell, diagnosis, tone, escalation): **`docs/TUTOR_CONSTITUTION.md`** is the source of truth; orchestrator and LLM prompts must align with it.

## Pedagogy and orchestrator

- The orchestrator decides pedagogy; the LLM only phrases. Never let LLM output decide correctness, next skill, mastery, or answer reveal.
- Every wrong answer passes `diagnosis.classify()` before a response is chosen (v2). No hint, check-your-work, or reveal without that path.
- Help escalates one level at a time: stuck-point (when implemented) → hint levels 1–2 (leak-checked, including step hints) → hint 3 is only the `reveal_solution` lead-in, never a retry hint.
- Reveal only after the attempt following hint 2 is wrong, or `show_solution` after two hints; then a different similar item. Offline must enforce the same rules.
- Never end a session immediately on a failure when caps allow one more success item (R40, v2).
- Item selection uses mastery/ladder and p_known tiers where applicable; authored difficulty is ordering only.
- Lesson beats, explain-back grades, and checkpoint scores never update BKT or FSRS. Checkpoint items are never used for teaching or practice.
- Exactly one BKT update per item, at the first answer or first help request. Later hinted-correct only increments `mastery.hinted_correct`.
- Mastery ladder levels require their evidence (v2); hinted correct does not reach “independent” levels; widget/interactive results are never trusted from the client — server re-checks predicates.

## Verifier and correctness

- Correctness comes from the allowlist verifier (and widget goal predicates when used), never the LLM or client. Never call `sympify` on raw student input.
- On sync, re-verify from stored response and ignore any client `correct` flag.

## LLM, grounding, and content

- No PII in LLM prompts or logs. Consent scopes gate features (`ai_processing`, `free_text`, `teacher_share`, `research_pseudonymised`, etc.).
- Explain-back grades are formative only. Without `ai_processing` or an API key: store the student’s text, show the authored explanation, give no grade. Never change mastery or FSRS.
- Study Mode / Ask (v2): factual statements cite approved passages or say out of scope; no web fallback. Unknown-licence content is never indexed.
- System must work end-to-end with no LLM key (authored content fallback).
- Do not machine-translate content and mark it approved; translations need a human reviewer.
- Production serves `status=approved` only unless `ALLOW_DRAFT_CONTENT=true`. Draft LLM output is never runtime content.

## Region-neutral (v2)

- No country, board, language, script, or time-zone literals in application code except in `config/`, `content/`, and tests. Use curriculum/locale/jurisdiction registries and profiles.
- Quiet hours and retention come from the jurisdiction profile, not hard-coded zones.

## Privacy, teachers, and research

- Teachers only see students with `teacher_share`. Comparison/checkpoint research machinery lives behind `RESEARCH_MODULE` when on.
- No dark patterns, ranks, or streak threats.

## Engineering

- Keep `policy`, `diagnosis`, `ladder`, and verifier/widget predicates pure and tested under `orchestrator/`, `learner/`, `verifier/`, and shared fixtures in `packages/shared/fixtures/`.
- Session actions expose orchestrator-owned flags (e.g. `can_request_hint`, `can_show_solution`); the client must not infer pedagogy from counters alone.
- Prefer simple, explicit code over clever abstractions; monolith first.
